WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.467
-Welcome, welcome,
welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.767
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:05.367
You're here, you made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:08.901
Thank you for watching.

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:10.868
Well, let's get to
some news here, guys.

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:12.601
This morning,
the world's richest man,

00:00:12.601 --> 00:00:17.033
Elon Musk, was named "Time"
magazine's Person of the Year.

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:18.434
Yeah.
Musk received the honor

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:20.400
for his work
in space exploration

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.601
and after he bought
10 million subscriptions

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:26.267
to "Time" magazine.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:27.767
I'm kidding.
Although it was a little strange

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:29.501
that everyone at "Time"
drove into work today

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:32.300
in a brand-new Tesla.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.267
Being named Person of the Year
is a big deal.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.000
It's basically
Sexiest Man Alive,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.334
but you're competing against
the Dalai Lama and the Pope.

00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:39.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:40.701
It was actually
a pretty competitive year.

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:42.167
The other finalists
were the scientists

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:44.801
behind the COVID vaccine
and the lawyer who appeared

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:46.501
at a Zoom trial
with a cat filter.

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:47.734
-Can you hear me, Judge?

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:50.100
I'm here live.
I'm not -- I'm not a cat.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:55.100
-Some news from Washington.
Today, President Biden signed

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.801
an executive order aimed at
improving customer experience

00:00:57.801 --> 00:01:00.400
for government services,
like renewing passports

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.567
and filing taxes.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:04.701
Yeah, now when you get audited,
the IRS agent

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:06.400
draws a little smiley face
on your return.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:09.968
And this is nice.
Now, when you're on hold

00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:11.601
for two hours,
instead of light jazz,

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:15.200
they play even lighter jazz.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.300
Hey, I saw that former
Vice President Mike Pence

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:20.234
has been touring key election
states, like New Hampshire.

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:21.801
A lot of people think
that he could be gearing up

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:24.367
for a presidential run in 2024.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:26.300
He's even been testing out
some campaign slogans

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:27.801
to see what people respond to.

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:30.767
Check some of these out.
First up, there's "Pence 2024 --

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:32.868
I make Mitt Romney
look like Post Malone."

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:35.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.534
Next, there's "Pence 2024 --
I call ketchup hot sauce."

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:43.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.534
And, finally,
there's "Pence 2024 --

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:47.234
One time, I heard
a Megan Thee Stallion song

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:49.334
and fainted."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:52.000
I think that's the one.
-Wow, yeah! That's the one.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.801
-"Mother!"
-"Mother!"

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:57.968
-Oh, I heard that,
in a new documentary,

00:01:57.968 --> 00:02:01.000
Russian President Vladimir Putin
revealed that, back in the '90s,

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.567
he worked as a cab driver
to make ends meet.

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:06.467
Yep, it was the only cab
where you got in,

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:08.000
and the driver told you
where you're going.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:12.234
"We're taking detour."
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:13.834
It was the last time Putin
drove a car

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:15.834
where the "passenger"
wasn't in the trunk.

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:18.167
[ Laughter, scattered groans ]

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:20.501
Hey, this is cool --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:23.000
-Wow!
-Listen to this.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.133
New FDA-approved eye drops
just hit the market

00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:29.267
that provide better vision
for up to 10 hours.

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:30.968
And they could replace
reading glasses

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:32.667
for millions of Americans.

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:34.501
Yeah, which means your dad
will now walk around

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:36.767
looking for the eye drops that
are on the top of his head.

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:39.934
[ Laughter ]
"Where did I put --"

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:41.200
You know some guy's
gonna be like,

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.267
"I bet if I use the whole
bottle, I could see Mars."

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:45.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:47.601
Now when you notice someone
putting in eye drops,

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:49.701
you can play the fun new game,
"Reader or Stoner?"

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:52.100
It's cool. It's fun.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.868
Well, get this --
authorities in New Zealand

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:55.934
are investigating after one man
apparently got

00:02:55.934 --> 00:03:00.434
10 COVID vaccine shots
on the same day

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:03.367
and pretended to be
a different person each time.

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:04.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:07.400
If you asked what he got,
he says, "Johnson and Johnson

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.934
and Johnson and Johnson
and Johnson and Johnson."

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:10.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:12.801
It was weird at his office
holiday party when he was like,

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:15.901
"So, how did you guys
feel after the ninth dose?

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:17.868
That one kind of got me."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:19.834
You guys hear about this?
A Michigan woman is currently

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:22.000
facing up to nine years
in prison

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.634
after she went to a fake website
called "Rent-A-Hitman"

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:29.634
and offered $5,000 to have
her ex-husband killed.

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:30.868
Yeah, you could tell
she was nervous.

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:33.534
Today, she logged into
Bribe-A-Judge.org.

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:35.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:38.200
And, finally, a man in Texas
has been getting some attention

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.601
for his Christmas light display.
Check this out.

00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:43.667
♪ Let me see you do it ♪
♪ Ay ♪

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:45.734
Hey!
♪ Snap your fingers ♪

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:47.133
♪ And then rock with it ♪

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:50.234
♪ Do it, do it, do it, do it,
gon' drop with it ♪

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:52.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:55.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.734
-Wow.

00:03:57.734 --> 00:03:59.300
I was expecting
an announcer to be like,

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.267
"And starting at point guard,
6'2", from Bethlehem..."

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:03.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.834 --> 00:04:05.801
At 10:00 p.m., the neighbors
asked him to turn it off,

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:07.734
and he was nice enough to say --
-"Okay!"

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:08.834
-There you go.

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:10.901
Guys, we have
exactly five shows left

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:12.701
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time

00:04:12.701 --> 00:04:14.601
for that beloved
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:17.200
It's time for
12 Days of Christmas Sweaters.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.334
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:20.601
-♪ 12 days
of Christmas sweaters ♪

00:04:20.601 --> 00:04:24.467
♪ 9 days left ♪

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:25.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:28.634
-That's right. Every show
between now and Christmas,

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.934
we'll be giving
one lucky audience member

00:04:30.934 --> 00:04:33.100
a mind-blowing Christmas sweater

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.033
from the
Countdown to Christmas Cabinet.

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:38.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.434
Now, since there
are five shows left,

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:43.167
let's open door number 5.
[ Drum roll ]

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:44.567
Oh, it's a big --
That's a tall one.

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:47.000
You got it, bud?
-[ Grunts ]

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.467
-Ooh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:52.300
♪♪

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.701
Whoa.

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:57.100
That is something else there.
Look at that.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.734
Wow. Let's see
the back of that guy.

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:04.133
It's like a -- It's a like
joker, type of jester.

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:07.033
It's got frills on the sleeves.

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:09.300
This is a great one.
This is a one-of-a-kind --

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.868
one-of-a-kind sweater.

00:05:10.868 --> 00:05:12.701
Let's see who's gonna go home
with tonight's sweater.

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:14.334
Everyone look
at your seat number.

00:05:14.334 --> 00:05:16.234
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:18.000
Who wants this sweater?
This is a good one.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:19.234 --> 00:05:20.734
Quest, can I get
a drum roll, please?

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:23.934
[ Drum roll ]

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:26.267
417!

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:29.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes!

00:05:29.968 --> 00:05:31.701
Come on down!
Come over here!

00:05:31.701 --> 00:05:35.133
♪♪

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:37.334
Hey!
-Oh, my God.

00:05:37.334 --> 00:05:39.534
-How are you?
-Great. Oh, my God.

00:05:39.534 --> 00:05:41.067
-What is your name,
and where are you from?

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:42.701
-Anthony.
I'm from Austin, Texas.

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:45.133
-Yes!
We love Austin.

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:47.400
We love Austin, Texas!

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.534
This will fit right in
in Austin.

00:05:49.534 --> 00:05:51.434
-Oh, yeah.
I'll blend in.

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:53.467
Yeah, I'll wear this to
the barbecue joints, yeah.

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:55.567
-Yes, you have to.
Would you like to try it on?

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:57.501
-Uh, yeah.
-What do you think, audience?

00:05:57.501 --> 00:05:59.033
You want to see him?
Yeah, there's --

00:05:59.033 --> 00:06:00.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I might need an assist.

00:06:00.334 --> 00:06:01.601
-I'll help you.
-Yeah, I don't know if there's

00:06:01.601 --> 00:06:04.734
a front or back.

00:06:04.734 --> 00:06:06.667
-Is there?
-There's no real right way

00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:08.167
to wear it, no.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:11.067
It's kind of a reversible.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:12.634
Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.634 --> 00:06:14.334
I mean, that's fantastic.

00:06:14.334 --> 00:06:16.200
Wow!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:20.434
Oh, my gosh.
That looks awesome!

00:06:20.434 --> 00:06:23.067
That looks so cool.

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:24.934
You already got a strut
to your step.

00:06:24.934 --> 00:06:26.734
I mean, this is fantastic.
All right.

00:06:26.734 --> 00:06:28.667
Well, take that back to Austin
with you and enjoy.

00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:30.234
-Thank you.
-Congratulations.

00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:31.634
Give another round of applause
for our winner.

00:06:31.634 --> 00:06:32.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
Stick around!

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:34.334
We're talking
with Dakota Johnson

00:06:34.334 --> 00:06:35.901
when we come back!
Everybody, come on back!

00:06:35.901 --> 00:06:37.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:37.868 --> 00:06:43.300
♪♪

